# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the checkout platform does.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text files
# to CRLF on checkout. A shell script that gets a carriage return on its shebang line fails
# on Linux with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", which is a confusing way to discover
# a line-ending problem on a cluster.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The LaTeX sources are edited on both platforms; normalise them in the repository.
*.tex text
*.py text
*.md text
